{"html":"<p>A React app is a tree of <strong>components</strong>: small functions that each describe a piece of the page. A product page might be a <code>Header</code>, a <code>ProductCard</code>, a <code>ReviewList</code> made of <code>Review</code>s, and a <code>Footer</code>. You build each piece once and reuse it with different data.</p>\n<h2 id=\"a-component-is-a-function\">A Component Is a Function</h2>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>Hello, Ana.&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>A component is a JavaScript function that returns what to show. Its name <strong>must start with a capital letter</strong>: <code>&lt;Greeting /&gt;</code> is a component, <code>&lt;greeting /&gt;</code> would be treated as an HTML tag.</p>\n<p>Use it like an HTML element, as many times as you want:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> App</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">main</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">main</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"jsx\">JSX</h2>\n<p>That HTML-looking syntax is <strong>JSX</strong>. It isn&#39;t HTML: a build tool turns it into JavaScript function calls that describe elements. So a few things differ from HTML:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>class</code> is <code>className</code>, and <code>for</code> is <code>htmlFor</code> (both are JavaScript keywords).</li>\n<li>Every tag must be closed: <code>&lt;img /&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;input /&gt;</code>.</li>\n<li>Attributes are camelCase: <code>onClick</code>, <code>tabIndex</code>.</li>\n<li>A component returns <strong>one</strong> root element. Wrap siblings in a fragment, <code>&lt;&gt;…&lt;/&gt;</code>, when you don&#39;t want an extra <code>div</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Inside JSX, <strong>curly braces</strong> run JavaScript:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    Hello, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">! You have </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">2</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> +</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 3</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> messages.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"props-passing-data-down\">Props: Passing Data Down</h2>\n<p>Components get data through <strong>props</strong>, like attributes on HTML elements. They arrive as one object, usually destructured:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">name</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">excited</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> false</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> }) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      Hello, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">      {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">excited </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">?</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \"!\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> :</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\"> \".\"</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ana\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> />          </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Hello, Ana.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Greeting</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Ben\"</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> excited</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> />  </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// Hello, Ben!</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Strings go in quotes; everything else goes in braces: <code>count={3}</code>, <code>user={user}</code>, <code>onSave={handleSave}</code>. A prop written alone, like <code>excited</code>, is <code>true</code>.</p>\n<p>Props are <strong>read-only</strong>. A component never changes its props: data flows <strong>down</strong>, from parent to child. To change something, the parent changes its own data and passes new props.</p>\n<h3 id=\"passing-functions\">Passing Functions</h3>\n<p>To let a child tell its parent something happened, pass a function:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">DeleteButton</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> onDelete</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">() </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> removeItem</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(item.id)</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>The child calls <code>onDelete()</code> when clicked; the parent decides what that means.</p>\n<h2 id=\"children\">children</h2>\n<p>Whatever you put <strong>between</strong> a component&#39;s tags arrives as the <code>children</code> prop:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Card</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">title</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">children</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> }) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">section</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">title</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">h2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">      {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">children</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">section</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Card</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> title</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"Shop\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ProductList</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> products</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">products</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> /></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Card</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>;</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>That&#39;s how layouts, modals and cards wrap any content.</p>\n<h2 id=\"lists-and-keys\">Lists and Keys</h2>\n<p>Turn an array into elements with <code>map</code>:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> ProductList</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">products</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> }) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ul</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">      {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">products.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">product</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">li</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> key</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">product.id</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">          {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">product.name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">: $</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">{</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">product.price</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">li</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      ))</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ul</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Each item needs a <strong><code>key</code></strong>: a value that&#39;s unique among its siblings and stable over time, usually the item&#39;s ID. React uses keys to match items between renders, so it can move, add or remove the right ones. Don&#39;t use the array index as key for lists that can reorder or shrink: state and inputs end up attached to the wrong item.</p>\n<h2 id=\"conditional-rendering\">Conditional Rendering</h2>\n<p>Three common patterns:</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> ProductList</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">({ </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">products</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> }) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (products.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> ===</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>No products yet.&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>; </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// early return</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ul</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">      {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">products.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">p</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=></span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">li</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> key</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">={</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">p.id</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">          {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">p.name</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">          {!</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">p.inStock </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x26;&#x26;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">span</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> (sold out)&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">span</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">/* show or nothing */</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">          {</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">p.onSale </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">?</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> &#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Badge</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">>Sale&#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">Badge</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">> </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">:</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> null</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> {</span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">/* one or the other */</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">        &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">li</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">      ))</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    &#x3C;/</span><span style=\"color:#116329;--shiki-dark:#7EE787\">ul</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  );</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Watch out for <code>{count &amp;&amp; &lt;Badge /&gt;}</code> when <code>count</code> can be <code>0</code>: React renders the <code>0</code>. Write <code>{count &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; &lt;Badge /&gt;}</code>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"splitting-into-components\">Splitting Into Components</h2>\n<p>When a component grows past a screen, or a part repeats, split it. Good components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>do <strong>one</strong> thing, with a name that says what (<code>PriceTag</code>, <code>ReviewList</code>),</li>\n<li>get everything they need through props,</li>\n<li>return the same output for the same props: easy to reuse and test.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-answer-in-short\">The Answer in Short</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>A component is a capitalized function that returns JSX.</li>\n<li>JSX looks like HTML but is JavaScript: <code>className</code>, closed tags, <code>{}</code> for expressions, one root element.</li>\n<li>Props pass data down, read-only; pass functions so children can report events.</li>\n<li><code>children</code> is whatever sits between a component&#39;s tags.</li>\n<li>Render lists with <code>map</code> and a stable, unique <code>key</code>, and use early returns, <code>&amp;&amp;</code> and <code>? :</code> for conditions.</li>\n</ol>\n"}